    "HaDeS MOSS Suite - Metadata (the fifth video tutorial)\n\nEvery MOSS Image Saver gets Suite Telemetry's json on metadata: the PNG carries the prompt, the settings,\nthe model and every LoRA with their hashes as A1111 parameters (what Civitai and image browsers read), the\nSuite's own copy of every node's settings (hades_moss) and ComfyUI's workflow (drop the PNG into ComfyUI).\n\nTwo samplers: with Telemetry on both stages the A1111 parameters are the first sampler's (1024, no denoise)\nand the Saver says so. The refined image's Saver also gets a second Telemetry (Refine stage) on\nprimary_stage_metadata, fed only by that stage: its PNG says 2048x2048, Denoising strength 0.25, and still\nkeeps the whole pipeline. The 1024 and x2 Savers get a Generate stage Telemetry the same way.\n\nModel: the file the KSampler's model comes from, with its hash; a merge made in the workflow is written\n'merge: a + b' without a model hash (Suite 0.9.3).\nPrivacy: hashes off removes the hashes, embed_workflow off removes the workflow; ComfyUI's\n--disable-metadata removes every text from the PNG.\nFile names: %model%, %seed%, %steps%, %cfg%, %sampler%, %width%, %height%, %date:...%.\n\nThe first save with hashes reads the model once (about 6 s for 10 GB here); later saves reuse it.\nMeasurements: tools/RESULTS.md in the HaDeS MOSS Suite."
   ],
   "properties": {}
  }
 ],
